{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1474164-humanity-morality-i-can-do-this-is-not-i-like-doing-this","id":1474164,"title":"Humanity / Morality: \"I can do this\" is not \" I like doing this\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-07T23:18:36-08:00","id":1474164,"title":"Humanity / Morality: \"I can do this\" is not \" I like doing this\"","content":"Most, if not all, very low morality characters ( 3 or less ) are depicted as actively killing, raping, maiming ecc.<br /> <br /> There's a thing that I feel is not discussed: that a person is <i>able</i> to do something without serious emotional repercussions do not means in any way that this person <i>likes </i>doing this thing.<br /> A person can be perfectly able to do something without hesitation or moral concerns, but still find it distasteful, boring, unpleasant, and the like; and of course, there are <b><i>consequences</i></b>.<br /> <br /> A silly personal example: I don't consider having a tooth removed by my dentist as immoral. I had to do that once ( a painful cavity ). I never had any regret or guilty feeling about.<br /> But I <i>definetly</i> didn't like it.<br /> <br /> A more serious personal example: when I was attending university at Trento, a drunken guy grabbed my by the throat. I headbutted him to get free. I never felt any sense of guilt about this, but it's nonetheless an unpleasant memory: I had to worry about this guy or his friends trying to get revenge in some ways, I changed the usual route to the university, and beside that I didn't sleep due adrenaline that night.<br /> <br /> So, in short, I think that a low morality / humanity person shouldn't <i>necessarily</i> be a serial / casual killer, rapist, ecc.<br /> <br /> If a low Humanity person also has other issues ( sadism, piromania, murderous obsessions ) , strong prejudices ( raging racism, homophobia, sexism, ecc. ) or extreme ideas ( religious or political fanaticism ) then he will probably act, and harm or kill people.<br /> <br /> If a low Humanity person finds himself in a situation where killing or harming is very profitable ( a large bribe or the opportunity to steal a vast amount of money ), necessary for survival ( kill to keep the last liter of water while lost in a desert ) or socially approved ( &quot;I was just following orders...&quot; ) then that person will probably act and kill.<br /> <br /> But if a low Humanity person is more or less mentally stable, and he finds himself in a social framework that makes violent crime disadvantageous and disapproved, I see no plausible reason for that people to go out of his way to kill.<br /> <br /> And, finally, were it's written that having a low Humanity means losing the self preservation instict?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T07:20:27-08:00","id":1474194,"title":"","content":"Note that most very low morality characters are supernatural beings that have supernatural forces actively pushing them towards insanity and/or depravation (usually in very self-destructive ways). Note that those splats that<i> do not</i>, also don't have a &quot;morality bar&quot; per se (albeit usualy have other things to worry about that may be tangentialy related to morals)<br /> <br /> Now, humans don't have that problem - but can be represented with Humanity in Vampire...so maybe what you say could stand true for humans.<br /> <br /> But, on that end, I have a doubt: <u>How much about capital M, Morality, it's really about <i>morality</i>?</u><br /> <br /> *Humanity as defined in Vampire isn't just about being good, but about acting as a human being. Note that Humans can't reach 0, to reach 0 you need to be under the influence of inhuman cravings. More so, Humanity 0 vampires can't care enough about social interaction to &quot;bath&quot; or have a long talk. They have survival instinct, but little more and can't really control themselves. That's why they need to be put down, they can't be trusted to keep the Masquerade, nor refrain from attacking their own allies - not even for their own good.<br /> <br /> *While Humanity it's defined on moral terms... one of best and more touching tragedies of the way it <i>works </i>in a vampire game it's that <i>a trully moral and good vampire</i> <i>can lose Humanity. </i>The way sins work, they don't care if you did the sin because you wanted or because you Frenzied. A vampire that's seriously a good person, but has problems (hasn't feed today - perhaps for ethical reasons, even. Or just &quot;it's a Brujah&quot;) could Frenzy and lose Humanity, while a stable sociopath that makes *sure* he won't ever sin because he fears loosing himself may be able to retain it.<br /> <br /> Maybe Humanity isn't that much about being good or remorseful about stuff. That's more a function of Conscience, perhaps. That's what <i>directly </i>makes you feel guilty. And, yes, that does help to retain Humanity (and it is very related with Humanity in other ways). It stands to reason to question to what extent Humanity it's about felling such guilt, and how much the guilt it's a tool to preserve your capability of being functional in human society<br /> <br /> Taking all of that in mind, if humans have Humanity (and if find humans having Humanity to be very questionable in the first place - they most certainly don't in games that aren't Vampire focused). I wonder how much about the lower echelons of Humanity/Road are including that whole caring about the social framework insofar as you *still* understand that your actions will have consequences. That perhaps someone with low humanity ain't just capable of remorseless sin, but has crossed the line already, and reached a point where it trully doesn't matter ... which would justify on the lowest end you have serial killers and so on.<br /> <br /> *Also, let's note that not all &quot;morality bars&quot; are representing the same thing. Paths/Roads clearly aren't about being a good boy (well, not most of them anyway), but about finding the internal strength and purpose to not surrender to the Beast. Mummies on Ma'at can be higly moral even at relatively low levels. Torment <i>goes up</i>, and some of the ways of raising it (like using certain powers) don't care about your ethics that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-08-2022, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T12:59:24-08:00","id":1474223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1474164-humanity-morality-i-can-do-this-is-not-i-like-doing-this?p=1474194#post1474194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Note that most very low morality characters are supernatural beings that have supernatural forces actively pushing them towards insanity and/or depravation (usually in very self-destructive ways). Note that those splats that</span></span></span><i> do not</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, also don't have a &quot;morality bar&quot; per se (albeit usualy have other things to worry about that may be tangentialy related to morals)</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, true. I should had addressed this issue too.<br /> Vampires and other supernaturals going berserk at low Humanity is justificated, storywise.<br /> <br /> I was thinking about low humanity / morality common mortals. Well, I was also thinking about both the old and the first edition new world of darkness. All the low morality humans I found are serial killers, slashers and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T01:20:44-08:00","id":1474265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1474164-humanity-morality-i-can-do-this-is-not-i-like-doing-this?p=1474223#post1474223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about low humanity / morality common mortals. Well, I was also thinking about both the old and the first edition new world of darkness. All the low morality humans I found are serial killers, slashers and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a sort of cherry picking/confirmation bias - if the mortal serial killers are statted with Humanity ratings, probably to compare them to vampires, then you're more likely to remember that. Whereas the 'common' mortals either won't have a Humanity stat (because its not needed) or possibly have a simple stat block without Humanity, then you're not going to remember that they didn't have it because real people are better at remembering what they see rather than what is not there.<br /> <br /> By the rules only Vampires should have a Humanity rating (I think). Morality is not part of the rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T13:42:31-08:00","id":1474323,"title":"","content":"Humanity/Path and Virtues in Vampire have one purpose - how effectively a vampire can keep the Beast at bay. A vampire with low Humanity/Path ratings is someone whom the Beast more easily controls. (To a real degree, the Path of Humanity is just as artificial as any Path of Enlightenment, it's just that it's a path that is easier to understand and therefore follow because the basics of it is a leftover from their life. What's important is the Path clearly acts as something that controls the Beast - it causes the vampire to say &quot;no&quot; to it.) As Humanity lessens, the Beast's influence grows on a vampire - it begins to effect the maximum number of Virtues that can be rolled, how hard it is to not appear like a corpse, how long a vampire remains in torpor, and so on (I am speaking of earlier edition rules here as I don't know V5).<br /> <br /> The problem for a low Humanity vampire, is that the vampire has difficulty realizing the difference between those things that feed the Beast and those that don't. Thus, he's more likely to let the Beast make decisions for him. At Humanity 0, it is only the Beast that makes these decisions. At that point, the vampire has no real personality, it's just a mask/persona the Beast uses (or completely abandons if it goes feral).<br /> <br /> Low Humanity vampires can do evil not because it's what they would wish to do, but because it's how the Beast might react in that situation. This is where we get to provocations for the purposes of Frenzy. Low Humanity means low Self-Control, as a vampire can't roll Virtues higher than their Humanity rating. So dealing with things like malicious taunts, harassment, physical provocations, humiliation, threats, etc. is much more hard. A vampire with high Humanity can deal with them like a living human would. A vampire with low Humanity is much more likely to react in accordance with what the Beast wants them to do - kill the person in order to eliminate the &quot;threat&quot;.<br /> <br /> A high Humanity vampire who acts in the grip of Frenzy should understand he lost control. He acted in a way contrary to his feelings. But a low Humanity vampire often lacks that self-awareness.<br /> <br /> While non-vampires in the game also have Humanity and Virtue ratings, they're essentially meaningless as humans don't have a Beast in them. However, you can see them as an example of what an equivalent vampire's Humanity if they did the same things this human did. So it's merely a comparison tool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T14:26:02-08:00","id":1474325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1474164-humanity-morality-i-can-do-this-is-not-i-like-doing-this?p=1474265#post1474265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the rules only Vampires should have a Humanity rating (I think).</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Revised book WOD: Mafia, normal human mobsters are still stated using the VtM Virtues and Humanity. Though there is some discussion in the book about narrative differences, the mechanics are the same.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------<br /> <br /> To the general point of the thread, I think one of the reasons most Humanity 1-3 people are painted as such horrible people is because you don't accidentally drop to that level of Humanity. Having Humanity 3 probably means you've killed a few people, and at least one to three of them were just cold blooded executions; not accidents, self-defense, crimes of passion, or whatnot. You're not going to fail every Humanity check and lose a dot each kill. A PC that's hit low Humanity has done a lot of nasty stuff, willingly.<br /> <br /> NPCs of course, also aren't usually written as if they were played out. The game authors just assign a value that feels right for the character.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T05:52:02-08:00","id":1474427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1474164-humanity-morality-i-can-do-this-is-not-i-like-doing-this?p=1474325#post1474325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the general point of the thread, I think one of the reasons most Humanity 1-3 people are painted as such horrible people is because you don't accidentally drop to that level of Humanity. Having Humanity 3 probably means you've killed a few people, and at least one to three of them were just cold blooded executions; not accidents, self-defense, crimes of passion, or whatnot. You're not going to fail every Humanity check and lose a dot each kill. A PC that's hit low Humanity has done a lot of nasty stuff, willingly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good explanation. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T02:30:38-08:00","id":1474796,"title":"","content":"Point of interest: Diablerie. <br /> <br /> If you're reading an older edition, Diablerie is just a way to kill someone. At most, you roll conscience for murder and there's no additional humanity penalty or trial for the act of draining a vampire to increase generation. <br /> If you're into anything revised or later, Diablerie is an automatic humanity loss, because you're feeding the Beast or consuming souls or something or other. It's heinously more evil than murder, and something that can have you lose two dots of humanity for action. Under post-revised diablerie rules, a relatively normal vampire can easily fall to 1/2/3/4 humanity after a couple of Diableries (but Ironically usually won't fall to 0 because players know there's no element of risk or gambling, they'll certainly fall to the beast if they do it one more time, so they won't) <br /> <br /> <br /> So, under this post-revised train of thought where &quot;feeding the beast&quot; can make you a worse person, would the beast have more influence over you at low humanity? After all, your virtue dice are capped by your humanity/path. Maybe once you get to humanity 1/2/3/4 your tastes and what satisfies you is influenced by the Beast. Maybe you should get willpower when you start doing sick shit rather than when you follow your nature I unsurprisingly heavily favour pre-revised rules for Diablerie, but even so I like the idea of offering low-humanity players willpower for indulging the beast more and perhaps giving them lesser willpower benefits for less degenerate efforts (though such efforts may aid them in restoring Humanity/Path)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T14:45:10-08:00","id":1475150,"title":"","content":"I think the vampire-like creatures in &quot;From&quot; are good examples of what vampires with little or no humanity are like. They don't technically lose intelligence, but they become so emotionally simple that it doesn't occur to them to use their intelligence for much besides a quick bit of low-grade cunning. Such a vampire might try to talk someone into inviting them in, but they can barely mask their eager leer. Their attempts at manipulation become extremely crude, because they can't remember what it's like to feel anything but hunger. They still try to manipulate with words, but since they are looking at their own memories of having complex emotions in a completely abstract way and trying to manipulate based on those abstract memories, the result wouldn't fool much of anyone if not backed up by Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}